# Generated files are gitignored (dir-local)

Full layout: [`docs/definitions/module.md`](../../docs/definitions/module.md).

**Package entry:** human `__init__.{impl_ext}`; generated = other
extensions of that stem only (`__init__.h`, `__init__.pyi`, …). Never
ignore/generate the human original’s own extension. Sibling stems
(`spin.rs`) get their own faces the same way.

**Ownership:** generated faces carry an in-file banner
(`DO NOT HAND-EDIT THIS FILE.`). That line is the write gate — sync
refuses to overwrite a file that exists without it. No `.generated/`
shadow tree.

**Rule:** anything `metal mod sync` writes must **not** be committed. Sync
maintains a **module-local** `.gitignore` managed block:

```gitignore
# BEGIN metal-generated
.target/
target/
__init__.h
__init__.pyi
__init__.toml
# END metal-generated
```

(Example for `impl=rs` with `--emit toml` — no `__init__.rs` line; that
file is human. `{stem}.toml` is listed only when that face was emitted.)

- The module `.gitignore` itself **is** committed.
- Do **not** hand-edit the managed block.
- Human `__init__.{ext}`, `.module`, ports stay tracked.
- Never ignore `Cargo.toml` via a blanket `*.toml` — only the stem face.
